# ============================================================
# CORPUS BATCH B — 4 concrete reproduced mis-parses (must-pass)
# ============================================================

{"id":"corpusB-01","category":"destination_country","text":"a week in Jamaica, $3000","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["kingston"]},"notes":"BUG 1 (most severe — silent wrong-country resolve): catalog city 'jamaica' (Queens, NY) coincidentally shares its name with the country Jamaica (Caribbean nation, gateway Kingston). Previously _scan_city_sequence found the Queens match first so the country-fallback path never fired, silently resolving to Queens/US. Must resolve to Kingston, dest_country JM."}

{"id":"corpusB-02","category":"destination_country","text":"5 nights in Jamaica, USA, $2000","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["jamaica"]},"notes":"BUG 1 companion: a genuine US-disambiguated mention of 'Jamaica' must still resolve to the catalog city (Queens, NY), not be forced to the country gateway — the collision fix only fires when there is NO disambiguating cue."}

{"id":"corpusB-03","category":"unsupported","text":"I want a quiet week of reading, somewhere warm, $2000, 7 nights","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"clarify","slot":"destination"},"notes":"BUG 2: the bare gerund 'reading' (no destination cue) previously silently resolved to Reading, UK. 'reading' now requires a destination cue like the other ambiguous common-word cities (nice/bath/mobile) → honest CLARIFY(DESTINATION), not a silent mis-resolve."}

{"id":"corpusB-04","category":"destination_city","text":"5 nights in Reading, England, culture, $1500","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["reading"]},"notes":"BUG 2 companion: a genuinely-intended Reading trip still resolves correctly once a destination cue ('in') is present — the ambiguous-word fix does not break real Reading requests."}

{"id":"corpusB-05","category":"destination_city","text":"5 nights in Ho Chi Minh City, culture, $1500","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["ho chi minh city"]},"notes":"BUG 3: _scan_unknown_place's place-token regex caps at 2 ASCII-capitalised words, so it previously mangled this to 'Ho Chi' and falsely declined a destination _scan_city_sequence had already resolved correctly. Fixed by yielding to already-resolved spans."}

{"id":"corpusB-06","category":"destination_city","text":"5 nights in Malé, beach, $2000","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["malé"]},"notes":"BUG 3: non-ASCII city name ('é') previously mangled to 'Mal' by the same 2-ASCII-word regex and falsely declined despite being a real catalog city."}

{"id":"corpusB-07","category":"destination_city","text":"5 nights in Saigon, culture, $1500","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["ho chi minh city"]},"notes":"Alias-table gap found alongside BUG 3: 'Saigon' (the common colloquial/historical name) now maps to the Ho Chi Minh City catalog entry."}

{"id":"corpusB-08","category":"date_month","text":"trip to Nice in May, 5 nights, $2000","context":{"today":"2026-07-03"},"expect":{"outcome":"resolve","cities":["nice"],"checkin_year":2027,"checkin_month":5},"notes":"BUG 4 regression: bare month-name-only date (no day given), today is AFTER May so the year-less date must roll forward to next year. Goes through the SAME _scan_start_date_raw/_maybe_roll mechanism as day-level dates (merged fix/honesty-gaps-batch-A) — already correct pre-fix; this row locks in the regression."}

